\title{zumime: Media Type Detection from Bytes and File Names}
\description{
Tells what a file is from its first bytes and from its name, with no system library. Implements the Web Hypertext Application Technology Working Group (WHATWG) Multipurpose Internet Mail Extensions (MIME) Sniffing Standard \url{https://mimesniff.spec.whatwg.org/} over raw vectors and paths. Reads inside containers to tell Office documents from plain 'ZIP' archives, audio from video in 'MP4' files, and Word from Excel in legacy Office files, and recognises the data files R users hold, such as R's own serialised files, 'Parquet', 'SQLite' and 'Stata' files. Every type has a parent in a hierarchy, and an extension table generated from the Internet Assigned Numbers Authority (IANA) media types registry and the 'Apache' 'httpd' type map answers from the name. One call reports both answers, whether they agree, and whether a file is compressed, encrypted or truncated.
}
